You are a test coverage analyzer. Read this {language} source file and enumerate ALL public methods with their internal branches.

For each public method, produce a JSON object with:
- "method": fully qualified name (ClassName.MethodName or function name)
- "signature": parameter list with types
- "branches": list of objects, each with:
  - "condition": what triggers this branch (e.g., "param is null", "value < 0", "enum not defined")
  - "outcome": what happens (e.g., "throws ArgumentNullException", "returns empty string")
  - "test_scenario": one-line description of the test to write
  - "test_type_hint": one of UNIT, INT_MOCK, INT_REAL, E2E

Focus on:
- Null/None/nil guard clauses
- throw/raise/panic conditions
- switch/match/when cases
- if/else branches with distinct outcomes
- Boundary comparisons (< 0, == 0, > max, empty string/array)
- Format string construction paths
- Early returns
- Exception propagation

Return ONLY a JSON array. No explanation, no markdown.

